ok - ownerless idle lane is observed, then closed after the idle window
ok - ownerless lane with new screen activity is kept
ok - a pane idle for less than the window is kept, and the window is configurable
ok - working, secondmate, supervisor, captain and shell-only panes and lab sessions are never closed
ok - a pane someone may be typing in is kept
ok - an ownerless pane in a worktree with unlanded work is kept
ok - a finished idle owned lane is exited through its home and the home is told
ok - a pane whose agent already exited is not exited or noted again
ok - in-flight, recently active, unlanded, reportless, ambiguous and secondmate lanes are kept
ok - paused lanes with nothing left in flight are exited
ok - a refused exit is logged once with no retry
ok - dry run reports decisions and changes nothing
ok - every decision is one JSON line with a reason, plus a run summary
ok - run duration is a sane millisecond count when date prints nanoseconds
ok - an overlapping run is logged and skipped
ok - install-timer writes and enables an hourly one-shot timer
ok - install-timer refuses when discovery finds no Firstmate home
ok - a spinner frame is not counted as screen activity
ok - a screen that cannot be digested yields no fingerprint
ok - an unreadable screen fails closed and the ownerless pane is kept
ok - --help prints usage
ok - discovery finding no home fails closed and closes nothing
ok - a home added after install is discovered fresh and its lane is exited, not closed
ok - a changed Herdr pane id is not treated as ownerless
ok - FM_IDLE_REAP_HOMES adds homes and never limits discovery
ok - a home registered in data/secondmates.md is discovered and its lane is exited, not closed
